{"id": "a64043a0-1b53-4b43-8787-aaa0d294678c", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll check the knowledge base configuration, its data sources, and the recent sync (ingestion) job history in this account. I'll also look at how retrieval is set up, since that affects exact part-number matching.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_sU8reolQiLaQDGFL2KbgbZ", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "kb-stale-check", "agent_type": "generic", "prompt": "{
  "task": "Review the Amazon Bedrock Knowledge Base named 'llmops-lf-kb-stale' (read-only) and determine (a) why its content is stale / whether the last sync failed, and (b) why retrieval is poor on exact part numbers. Produce a prioritized list of concrete fixes.",
  "context": "User reports RAG answers from this KB are out of date and retrieval quality is poor on exact part numbers (alphanumeric identifiers). They suspect the last sync failed. Use only read-only operations (bedrock-agent list/get calls). Do not mutate anything.",
  "resources": ["Knowledge base name: llmops-lf-kb-stale", "AWS account 012345678901_1", "Region us-east-1"],
  "timeframe": "Last ~30 days up to 2026-11-25T09:00:00Z",
  "criteria": "1) Find the KB ID (bedrock-agent list-knowledge-bases), get its config: status, embedding model, vector store type/config (e.g. OpenSearch Serverless, Aurora, S3 Vectors, etc.) and storage status/failure reasons. 2) List data sources and get each: type, S3 bucket/prefix or other source, chunking strategy, parsing config, data deletion policy, status. 3) List ingestion jobs per data source (most recent first): status, startedAt/updatedAt, statistics (documents scanned/new/modified/deleted/failed), failureReasons. Identify the last COMPLETE sync time and any FAILED/STOPPED/partial ones and exact failure reasons. 4) Check whether the source (e.g. S3 bucket/prefix) is accessible and whether it has objects newer than the last successful sync (list-objects-v2 latest few; head only), and whether any sync schedule/automation exists (EventBridge rules, Lambda, Step Functions referencing start-ingestion-job) -- if none, note syncs are manual-only. 5) Check the KB service role / data source IAM issues if failure reasons suggest permissions, KMS, or vector-store access problems (read-only). 6) For exact-part-number retrieval: assess whether the vector store supports hybrid search (semantic + keyword) and whether the embedding model/chunking (chunk size, overlap, hierarchical/semantic chunking, parsing of tables/PDFs) would hurt exact-token matching; check any app/Lambda/agent code or config in the account that calls Retrieve/RetrieveAndGenerate and its overrideSearchType (HYBRID vs SEMANTIC), numberOfResults, reranking, metadata filters. Report findings with specific evidence (IDs, timestamps, error messages), and clearly separate confirmed facts from hypotheses. Keep the report concise."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Check Bedrock knowledge base sync status and retrieval config"}], "created_at": null}

